    "category": "backtest_claim",
    "excerpt": "When Bitcoin's price falls below its 200-week moving average, it often indicates a potential buying opportunity \u2026 Investors can set buy orders to trigger automatically when Bitcoin's price drops below this threshold. \u2026 Investing $10,000 during the March 2020 dip would have resulted in a 1.8 BTC / $105,000 portfolio today \u2026 but if you missed that opportunity, you would have had to wait until June 2022",
    "performance_claim": "Investing $10,000 during the March 2020 dip would have resulted in a 1.8 BTC / $105,000 portfolio today",
    "verbatim_confidence": "high",
    "notes": "Buy below 200-week MA (1400 daily bars), no exit; anecdotal single-trade claim. Same post also mentions fear&greed/rainbow (excluded from excerpt)."
  },
